# Cross-frame DivByZero drop-correctness (error-model.md §11, Increment 2.1c, Q9
# — the subtlest property): the callee `q`'s frame holds a LIVE Drop-bearing
# local (`g`, a Guard with a custom drop) when the div0 happens. The fault
# propagates to `main`'s catch one frame up; the callee's early-exit drops run on
# the fault path, so `g` is dropped EXACTLY ONCE. The deterministic "drop guard N"
# print proves exactly-once on BOTH the fault path AND the no-fault path. Run
# under ASan/UBSan: clean (no leak, no double-free).
struct Guard:
    int id

equip Guard with Drop:
    void drop(!self):
        print(f"drop guard {self.id}")

# `g` is live (its field feeds the divide) when `a / b` may div0. On the fault
# path the early-exit drops free `g` once; on the no-fault path scope-exit frees
# it once. Block-body form so the Guard local is in the callee frame.
int q(int a, int b, int gid):
    Guard g = Guard(gid)
    int r = a / b + g.id
    return r

void main():
    int z = 0
    int caught = q(10, z, 1) catch Fault.DivByZero: -1
    print(f"{caught}")                       # fault path → -1 (after "drop guard 1")
    int ok = q(20, 4, 2) catch Fault.DivByZero: -1
    print(f"{ok}")                           # no-fault path → 20/4 + 2 = 7 (drop guard 2)
